# E-ink dark terminal LS_COLORS
# On e-ink, color luminance maps to gray level — blue/red are nearly invisible on black.
# Strategy: use white/yellow (high luminance) for important types, avoid blue entirely.
#
# ANSI luminance on dark bg (approx): white=100% yellow=90% cyan=70% green=50% red=30% blue=10%

RESET 0
DIR 01;37           # directories      → bold white   (was bold blue — nearly invisible)
LINK 01;36          # symlinks         → bold cyan
MULTIHARDLINK 00;37 # hard links       → white
FIFO 01;33          # named pipes      → bold yellow
SOCK 01;33          # sockets          → bold yellow
DOOR 01;33          # doors            → bold yellow
BLK 01;33           # block devices    → bold yellow
CHR 01;33           # char devices     → bold yellow
ORPHAN 07;37        # broken symlinks  → reverse white
MISSING 07;37       # missing targets  → reverse white
EXEC 01;33          # executables      → bold yellow  (was bold green)
SETUID 07;37        # setuid           → reverse white
SETGID 07;37        # setgid           → reverse white
STICKY_OTHER_WRITABLE 07;37
OTHER_WRITABLE 07;37
STICKY 07;37

